  "notes": {
    "content": [
      "The page compares family F, collection M and collection L as underlying sets for an axiomatics of ateliers: simplest data on F, most transparent essential axioms on L, with a question about M.",
      "Display (1.16) gives three proposed primitive structures on family F. Its right annotation names the deployment map F ↦ tilde F. The lower brace explains incidence by F ∈ M and F ≤ G.",
      "A later dated note points to b) and says that under the author’s new viewpoint it no longer implies ≪.",
      "The final paragraph announces a diagram of six fundamental relations and defines incidence with triangleleft in (1.17). No six-relation diagram is actually drawn on this page."
    ],
    "math_reading_decisions": [
      "The straight-underbar relation is ≤, the double straight angles are ≪, and the curved relation with curved lower rule is preccurlyeq. No M indices appear under these signs here.",
      "The map between collections has a plain right arrow; the element map has an initial upright and a wave over its target F.",
      "P has a plain upright stem and upper bowl without a distinct lower calligraphic return on this page; upright P is a local reading, not a correction of other pages.",
      "The underbrace begins beneath et and the map, not under the preceding ≪. It is explanatory formula layout, not a separate diagram.",
      "Both incidence conditions literally use F ∈ M and F ≤ G; this visual agreement is not a mathematical proof.",
      "The closed left-pointing triangle and double equivalence arrow are preserved with dfn above and a tentative lower par.",
      "The literal le plus transparent and unresolved adjective number are preserved without grammatical normalization."
    ],
    "author_doubts": [
      "(ou peut-être pareil pour M ?)",
      "(20. juin) Non, par mon nouveau point de vue ça n'implique plus ≪"
    ],
    "titles_dates_counts": [
      "Underlined title: Axiomes. Underlined lead-in: Sur family-F.",
      "Author’s manuscript page 10; supplied scan 11. No separate archive pencil sheet number observed.",
      "Labels (1.16) and (1.17); three choices a), b), c); six relations announced.",
      "Literal date (20. juin), including point after 20; no year supplied.",
      "Actual views: one whole, two supplied halves, thirteen enhanced crops. No image viewed twice."
    ]
